type FrontierQualifiedModuleBinding {
  module_path: String
  qualified_module: String
}

type CompilerFrontierAttributedDebt {
  dissolution_trigger: Symbol
}

type CompilerFrontierCensusAttribution
  = KnowledgeAttributed { dissolution_trigger: Symbol }
  | ExecutionMeasured {
      probe_kernel_receipt: Symbol,
      wave_label: Symbol,
      blocker_class_distribution: CompilerFrontierAttributedDebt,
      gap_clustering: CompilerFrontierAttributedDebt
    }

data compiler_frontier_blocker_class_distribution_attribution: CompilerFrontierAttributedDebt = CompilerFrontierAttributedDebt {
  dissolution_trigger: ^migrate_when_frontier_per_module_probe_receipt_binds
}

data compiler_frontier_gap_clustering_attribution: CompilerFrontierAttributedDebt = CompilerFrontierAttributedDebt {
  dissolution_trigger: ^migrate_when_frontier_located_reason_survey_binds
}

data compiler_frontier_census_attribution: CompilerFrontierCensusAttribution = ExecutionMeasured {
  probe_kernel_receipt: ^frontier_classify_unlisted_reason_refuses_holds,
  wave_label: ^wave2_post_resolver_6451_body_stage_a_6443,
  blocker_class_distribution: compiler_frontier_blocker_class_distribution_attribution,
  gap_clustering: compiler_frontier_gap_clustering_attribution
}

data compiler_frontier_probe_kernel_receipt_note: String = "probe_kernel_receipt binds the fail-closed classifier RED control (frontier_classify_unlisted_reason_refuses_holds), not per-module frontier_probe_emit_from_ingest execution. Structural census invariants are compiler_frontier_structural_census_invariants_holds; per-module receipts deferred via CompilerFrontierAttributedDebt dissolution triggers."

type SelfHostFrontierDisposition
  = SelfEmitted
  | SeedRetained { reason: Symbol, migration_trigger: Symbol }

type CompilerModuleFrontierRow {
  module_path: String
  disposition: SelfHostFrontierDisposition
  measured_probe: FrontierProbeReceipt
  tractability_rank: Int
}

data compiler_frontier_self_emitted_baseline_ratchet_note: String = "Class-5 carve-out: this baseline is a progress ratchet on SelfEmitted disposition count, not a duplicate of roster length. compiler_frontier_self_emitted_count() filters the roster by disposition; the baseline is an independent floor that reds when modules silently regress SelfEmitted -> SeedRetained. Deriving it from the same filter would tautologize the check (same rule as languages_consumer_census and test_migration_debt ratchets)."

data compiler_frontier_self_emitted_baseline: Int = 6

data compiler_frontier_binding_hand_rows_note: String = "THE SECOND AUTHORITY, still live for ONE consumer and gated because of it. These 27 rows no longer serve the witness path — that projects off the derived ModuleStorageIndex — but they still feed the crate-layout EMITTER, which cannot be handed a host index without polluting an unrelated 18-variant dispatch (frontier_emitter_hand_row_debt_note has the full reasoning and the count).

So two representations of the path⇄module fact are live at once, which §3 forbids in general. What makes this an honest interim rather than a fork is that they are PARITY-GATED: transition_parity_host_index_agrees_with_hand_rows is a STANDING witness on the wet cadence (promoted from one-time transition receipt, parent ruling 2026-07-19) asserting that the derived index and these rows answer identically for every path the rows name. If they ever drift, that witness REDS.

That promotion is the point. As a one-time switchover check it would have proven the two agreed at a moment and said nothing afterwards, leaving a silent fork behind it. As a standing check it IS the §3 protection for as long as the duality lives — the mechanism that makes 'both exist' safe rather than merely admitted.

It still catches both original failures — a projection bug (derivation disagrees with a known-good table) and hand-row drift (the table went stale and the derivation is right) — told apart by inspecting which side is wrong.

dissolve-on: host-driven generation of the crate-layout artifact with the index supplied at the boundary. At that point this block, FrontierQualifiedModuleBinding, the _hand_rows fn family, and the parity witness are DELETED together — keeping any of them 'just in case' would restore the fork the parity gate exists to police."

